    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "NOVAworks has not been able to increase the long-term career mobility of enough\r\nvulnerable workers in its area of service. We identified two main underlying reasons for this\r\nchallenge. Firstly, NOVAworks has faced difficulty in registering vulnerable workers as\r\ncustomers, due to a lack of awareness of NOVAworks’s programs, a lack of trust in a successful\r\noutcome, and resource barriers to participating in a workforce development program. Secondly,\r\nthe workforce development system focuses on unemployment, rather than underemployment and\r\nworking poverty, which require different lenses through which to operate.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Hernandez, D., Li, K., and Richter, J. (2022). Social Capital for Workforce Development in San Mateo and Santa Clara Counties. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/zm859hp5094",
